% SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
% =====================================================================
% queries.clausal -- QUERY-COMBINATOR layer for eu/dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management.
% A TOP-LAYER consumer: it imports the determination slice's PUBLIC
% predicates it calls (and the profile readers), and nothing else.
%
% dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_profile_keys/1: the profile key schema, in
%     root_exports / input_contract order.
% dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_input_problems/2: the problems a profile has
%     ([] = none), re-exported from the kernel as the scaffold wrote it.
% dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_what_if/4 (#16 what-if): override one key,
%     then re-evaluate the verdict status. The profile is an ATTRIBUTE LIST, not a
%     dict, so the override is written here for attribute lists (kit override_key/4
%     takes a dict and raises type_error(dict, ...) on an attribute list): a present
%     key has its value replaced, an absent key is added.
% dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_compliance_check/4 (#13 compliance_check):
%     may the entity certify a duty (certify_duty(DutyAtom)) or all the
%     duties of RTS Articles 1 to 3 (certify_all_duties) in the current
%     state? permitted when the duty is judged performed (or every duty is,
%     the complete answer), prohibited when it is judged not performed (or
%     the duties are incomplete, or the entity is one of DORA Art 16(1), to
%     which Title II does not apply). Otherwise the status compound the
%     limbs give: indeterminate([Key]), needs_legal_review(...) or
%     input_problems(...), each with Citations [].
%
% #2 eligibility and #7 justification are served by the slice's facade
% (decide_*/2, *_status/2 and the cited *_checklist/2).
%
% ROOT EXPORTS: the result atoms, the judgement value unsure, the
% twenty-seven duty atoms and the twenty-eight profile key atoms are served
% here as 0-arity facts, so the package root carries each of them. The
% result constructors are DATA: they stay in the export list, have no
% clauses, and their fields are named by the constructors/1 declaration.
%
% Every predicate here decides nothing statutory of its own: it re-reads
% the answers the slice decided (with their implements/1 markers there).
% =====================================================================

:- module(queries, [
    dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_profile_keys/1,
    dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_input_problems/2,
    dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_what_if/4,
    dora_rts_policies_and_risk_management_compliance_check/4,
